.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt OESLOGGER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oeslogger
.Nd log OpenEndpointSecurity events as JSON
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dinp
.Op Fl j Ar jail | Fl J Ar jail
.Op Fl m Ar path
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Ar event_type ...
.Nm
.Fl l
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a passive
.Xr oes 4
client which writes observed security events as newline-delimited JSON.
With no event types it subscribes to all notification events.
Named event types restrict the subscription, for example
.Cm exec ,
.Cm open ,
.Cm create ,
.Cm unlink ,
.Cm fork ,
and
.Cm exit .
.Pp
.Nm
never authorizes or blocks an operation.
It uses notification mode and, by default, mutes itself and
.Pa /dev/
to reduce recursive and device noise.
Those defaults are ordinary mutable client state.
Each JSON record includes message IDs and sequence numbers, monotonic and
wall-clock timestamps, authorization results and deadlines, source process,
thread and path metadata, and event-specific objects.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Use a descendants-scoped client.
The logger process and its descendant subtree remain visible while unrelated
processes are hidden.
.It Fl i
With
.Fl j
or
.Fl J ,
also log signal, ptrace and scheduling events that a process outside the
jail directs at a process inside it.
The process recorded as the source of such an event is outside the jail.
.It Fl j Ar jail
Log only events of processes in the jail
.Ar jail
and in the jails nested beneath it.
.Ar jail
is a jail ID if it consists only of digits and a jail name otherwise; the
name of a nested jail is written with its parents, for example
.Li web.db .
Filtering is done by the kernel
.Pq see Xr oes 4 ,
so events of other processes are never delivered to
.Nm .
A process is logged while it is in the jail, including processes that enter
it later with
.Xr jexec 8 .
.It Fl J Ar jail
Like
.Fl j ,
but log only the named jail itself, not the jails nested beneath it.
.It Fl l
List accepted event names and exit.
.It Fl m Ar path
Mute events whose primary object has the given path prefix.
This option may be repeated.
.It Fl n
Disable the normal noise mutes and clear kernel-configured default process and
path mutes.
.It Fl o Ar file
Append JSON output to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.It Fl p
Pretty-print JSON instead of emitting one compact object per line.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fl d ,
.Fl j
and
.Fl J
options are mutually exclusive.
Each process object in the output carries
.Dq jid ,
the jail ID, and for a jailed process
.Dq jail_fullname ,
the jail's hierarchical name as seen from the host, which together identify
the nested jail a record came from;
.Dq jailname
is the jail's host name.
.Pp
The jail is resolved once, when
.Nm
starts.
If it does not exist or is being removed,
.Nm
exits with status 66
.Pq Dv EX_NOINPUT .
If the jail is removed while
.Nm
is running,
.Nm
writes the events the jail generated before its removal, reports the removal
on standard error and exits with status 0.
It does not wait for another jail of the same name or ID: that would be a
different jail.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 64
.Pq Dv EX_USAGE .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Log all observable events:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger
.Ed
.Pp
Log selected events to a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger -o /var/log/oes.ndjson exec open create unlink
.Ed
.Pp
Observe only the logger's process subtree without default noise filters:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger -d -n exec open
.Ed
.Pp
Log what happens in one container, nested jails included:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger -j web -o /var/log/web.ndjson exec open socket_connect
.Ed
.Pp
Format the normal NDJSON output with
.Xr jq 1 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oeslogger exec open | jq .
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jq 1 ,
.Xr liboes 3 ,
.Xr oes 4 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr jexec 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was added as the OpenEndpointSecurity event logging tool in
.Dx 16.0 .
